# FCPI M1 secrets: names, owners and modes only. No value ever enters Git.
# scripts/m1/pi-init.sh generates each missing file ON the Pi and never overwrites one.
# Directory /etc/firecrawl-pi/secrets is root:root 0700; every file is 0600.
# The owner is the uid that reads the file inside its container. Each service has a
# dedicated uid equal to its port; the images' default 999 is pihole on this host.
#
# name                      owner        consumer
postgres_password           5432:5432    nuq-postgres entrypoint (POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE, runs as uid 5432)
core_postgres_password      0:0          firecrawl-core wrapper (root) -> POSTGRES_PASSWORD for role fcpi_core (not the superuser's)
postgres_core_role_password 5432:5432    nuq-postgres initdb (020-fcpi-core-role.sh) sets fcpi_core's password; same value as core_postgres_password
rabbitmq_default_user_conf  5672:5672    rabbitmq conf.d fragment: default_user/default_pass for the first boot
redis_users_acl             6379:6379    redis-server aclfile: 'default' user by SHA-256 of the password; 'health' may only PING.
#                                        Known width: 'default' has +@all (incl. CONFIG, DEBUG, FLUSHALL); narrow it
#                                        against the command set M8's soak measures, not by guesswork (REVIEW.md R11).
core_redis_url              0:0          firecrawl-core wrapper -> REDIS_URL, REDIS_RATE_LIMIT_URL
core_nuq_rabbitmq_url       0:0          firecrawl-core wrapper -> NUQ_RABBITMQ_URL
gateway_token_hashes        3380:3380    M1's gateway registry ('<label> sha256:<hex>'); unmounted since M3, which reads gateway/clients
clients/m1-verify.token     0:0          plaintext client token for scripts/m1 verification; not mounted into any container, and not in M3's registry
#
# Also generated once, outside this directory:
#   /srv/firecrawl-pi/data/rabbitmq/.erlang.cookie   5672:5672 0400  (stable node identity; private)
#   /srv/firecrawl-pi/data/.fcpi-data-id            0:0     0644  (the project data ID; not a secret)
#
# M2 (scripts/m2/pi-init-m2.sh; created in pairs from one generated value, never overwritten)
retrieval_postgres_password       3310:3310  retrieval-service -> role fcpi_retrieval (DML on schema fcpi_retrieval only)
postgres_retrieval_role_password  5432:5432  nuq-postgres initdb (030-fcpi-retrieval.sh); same value as retrieval_postgres_password
core_retrieval_token              0:0        firecrawl-core wrapper (root) -> PI_RETRIEVAL_TOKEN, the core's credential for the retrieval service
retrieval_core_token_sha256       3310:3310  retrieval-service: 'sha256:<hex>' of core_retrieval_token; never the plaintext
retrieval_browser_token           3310:3310  retrieval-service -> its credential for the browser worker
browser_token_sha256              3320:3320  browser-worker: 'sha256:<hex>' of retrieval_browser_token; never the plaintext
#
# Also, outside this directory (not secrets):
#   /etc/firecrawl-pi/egress-local/egress-local.cidrs   0:0 0644  the host's connected networks (fcpi-egress-local.sh)
#
# M3 (scripts/m3/pi-init-m3.sh; the pair is created from one generated value, never overwritten)
gateway_postgres_password       3380:3380  access-gateway -> role fcpi_gateway (DML on schema fcpi_platform, EXECUTE on its marker lookup)
postgres_gateway_role_password  5432:5432  nuq-postgres initdb (040-fcpi-platform.sh); same value as gateway_postgres_password
gateway/                        3380:3380 0700  directory mounted into the gateway; replaced files are seen at once
gateway/clients                 3380:3380  the client registry: '<label> <principal> <scopes> sha256:<hex>' lines, written only by
#                                          scripts/m3/pi-client-token.sh; never a plaintext token
clients/<label>.token           0:0        a client's plaintext gateway token (fcpi_<label>_<64 hex>), created by pi-client-token.sh for the
#                                          owner to give that client; mounted into no container
#
# Also, outside this directory (not secrets):
#   /srv/firecrawl-pi/data/artifacts/                   3380:3380 0700  archived results (content-addressed), on the data mount
#   /srv/firecrawl-pi/data/artifacts/.fcpi-artifact-root 3380:3380 0600  the data ID; without it the gateway will not start
#
# M5 (scripts/m5/pi-init-m5.sh; each pair is created from one generated value, never overwritten)
gateway_retrieval_token         3380:3380  access-gateway -> its credential for the retrieval service's extraction listener (fcpi_model)
retrieval_gateway_token_sha256  3310:3310  retrieval-service: 'sha256:<hex>' of gateway_retrieval_token; never the plaintext
searxng_proxy_password          3330:3330  searxng -> its credential for the retrieval service's search proxy (fcpi_search)
retrieval_searxng_proxy_sha256  3310:3310  retrieval-service: 'sha256:<hex>' of searxng_proxy_password; never the plaintext
searxng_secret_key              3330:3330  searxng: its server secret (SEARXNG_SECRET)
providers/                      3310:3310 0700  directory mounted read-only into the retrieval service; a key placed later needs no recreation
# Provider credentials (FIRECRAWL_PI_SPEC.md §36), placed only by scripts/m5/pi-provider-key.sh from stdin, one
# file each, 3310:3310 0600. Absent, the provider is BLOCKED_CREDENTIAL (a model) or PARSER_REQUIRED (the
# parser); present, it is still refused while PI_PAID_DISPATCH_ENABLED=false or its caps in
# deploy/policies/budget.json are zero. A key is never an authorization to spend (CLAUDE.md §11).
providers/anthropic_api_key     3310:3310  Anthropic, the default extraction model claude-haiku-5-5 (budget.json providers.anthropic)
providers/agent_anthropic_api_key 3310:3310  Anthropic, the playground Agent's model claude-opus-5-5 (budget.json providers.anthropic-agent); a separate key, so the Agent's spend is its own
providers/llamaparse_api_key    3310:3310  LlamaParse, the complex-document parser (budget.json providers.llamaparse)
providers/decodo_proxy          3310:3310  M6: the Decodo residential proxy's '<proxy username>:<password>' (budget.json providers.decodo); a sub-user
#                                          used by this deployment alone, so its usage report is this deployment's traffic
providers/decodo_api_key        3310:3310  M6: Decodo's public API key, read only for the usage report that reconciles proxy bytes
#
# M6 (scripts/m6/pi-init-m6.sh; the pair is created from one generated value, never overwritten)
providers/fixture_proxy         3310:3310  the fixture proxy's '<name>:<password>', which the retrieval service presents (unpaid, fixture network only)
fixture_proxy_sha256            8080:8080  fixture-m6: the SHA-256 of providers/fixture_proxy, which its proxy checks
#
# M7 (scripts/m7/pi-init-m7.sh; each pair is created from one generated value, never overwritten)
webhook_signing_secret          3310:3310  retrieval-service: the key every webhook delivery is signed with (HMAC-SHA256)
fixture_webhook_secret          8080:8080  fixture-m7: the receiver's own copy of webhook_signing_secret, which it verifies deliveries with
providers/fixture_zyte           3310:3310  the fixture enhanced provider's key, which the retrieval service presents (unpaid, fixture network only)
fixture_zyte_sha256             8080:8080  fixture-m7: the SHA-256 of providers/fixture_zyte, which its provider checks
providers/zyte_api_key          3310:3310  M7: Zyte API's key (budget.json providers.zyte), placed only by scripts/m5/pi-provider-key.sh; never an
#                                          authorization to spend: its caps are zero and paid dispatch is off until the owner approves
#
# Also, outside this directory (not secrets):
#   /etc/firecrawl-pi/selection/selection.json     0:0 0644  the host's selection of search engines, model and parser
#                                                            (scripts/m5/pi-selection.sh; retrieval service reads it every minute)
